"Ancient chords of long-forgotten lamentations still echo in Orr. Those who have learned to listen for them are able to use dirges of power, making manifest abilities once lost to the pages of history.",
"Ancient druids had the power to manipulate nature. Learn this Mastery to gather Oakheart's essence, which allows you to grapple to new heights using magical vines.",
"Ancient magics still linger in the world of Tyria, and those especially attuned to them can sometimes call on them in times of great need. Learn this mastery to unlock an extra skill for use while downed.",
And Stay Dead,
And a choice of:,
And another surprise gift box!,
And feel your vow shatter like their mortal bones.,
"And here I thought this camp would never run smoothly. The lowlanders have come to this place from time to time to hunt, but never have we used it as a base of operations. We're very much in your debt, Wayfinder.",
"And here, the bloodshed is so potent, a taste of foul iron taints your tongue,",
"And the folks at the smithy love anyone who isn't afraid to get their hands dirty. If you're up for making metal out of ore, I would suggest talking to Bronzed Sun.",
"And their deepest fear is others knowing they're afraid,",
"And then we have our surveys. First, a small contingent of our allies have begun using a bloodstone golem to assist in maneuvering through the deadly valley we've been having trouble navigating.",
And there's also plenty of Inquest and hostile wildlife to contend with.,
And this round goes to...,
"And we have succeeded, as we succeed in everything we turn our attention to.",
And we must act.,
"And yet, I know failure. I challenged my lifelong rival to fight at a moot, and in my overconfidence, I lost. I look forward to the day when I can even the score.",
"And yet, in the past, I have been foolish. I wagered Romke's Horn, an ancestral heirloom with magical properties, on a test of strength. I was overconfident, but I'm determined to get it back.",
"And yet, in the past, I've been careless. I overindulged in merriment at a moot and woke up the next morning with no memory of what I'd done. It's a mystery I must solve.",
"Ander ""Wildman"" Westward",
