Captain Saia's Journal,
"Captain Sayida,  

Now that proper communication and supply channels have been established with the Castoran expedition, Empress Ihn has requisitioned a refresh of jade tech supplies. That jade tech might play any role in overcoming the brutality of Inquest magitech is a point of pride—or rather, those were Lady Joon's words. I've no doubt that Xunlai Jade has their own interest in studying the seers' magical infrastructure in full when this whole Inquest mess is over.  

On a more concerning note, there's been chatter in my circles that the detained ""gift"" sent back by the alliance's kestrel delegate never made it into MinSec custody. Minister Cho Min of MinSec is considering bringing in some outside assets to investigate, and I may reinforce that notion if I have the chance. Still, it could be some time before they pick up a trail.  

Otherwise, I hope Rytlock and Canach aren't causing you too much trouble; those two always seem to end up in some mess or another when the commander's involved.  

Give them my regards,  
Ambassador Kasmeer Meade",
"Captain Sylvour Denwatcher,

Firstly I hope you are well, old friend. I know these days are dire.  
  
I will keep this brief. I am writing to inquire about one of your inmates. A certain...suave sylvari, if I'm to believe the rumors. I've done my research, and I see that he's led a tumultuous and storied life so far: involuntary test subject, Consortium cartographer and project team leader, Molten Facility liberator, and corporate saboteur. For all his struggles, he's developed something of a reputation, even in the quieter halls of Divinity's Reach. And as it turns out, I have use for a man of his particular ""prestige"" and skillset.  
  
There are places I cannot move through without notice and things I cannot do from my current station without drawing unwanted attention, so I've learned to delegate more effectively. In this case, he would serve as an...extension of the Shining Blade and the Krytan crown—under my express supervision, of course. If you think he'd be at all cooperative, I am interested in purchasing his billet.  
  
Thank you for your time,  
  
Countess Anise, Exemplar of the Shining Blade",
"Captain Tervelan said the letters he received were signed by Minister Arton. If Arton ordered the Falcon Company's deaths, then he's a danger to Queen Jennah—and he's working against the treaty at Ebonhawke. He must be stopped.",
"Captain Thackeray has been a friend, and shown a genuine interest in your well-being. He said he'd keep an eye out for ways you could help Divinity's Reach. Time to check in and see if you can lend a hand.",
"Captain Thackeray protects the city of Divinity's Reach, and guards Queen Jennah from harm. If there's trouble, he knows to call on you. Your friendship is a source of strength for both of you.",
