Citizen's Co-operative,
"Citizen,

The streets of Lion's Arch are quiet in the wake of the events at Dragon Bash. While the festival didn't go as well as planned, Lion's Arch is still standing. You helped protect our fair city, so you have my thanks.

Clear skies,
Captain Magnus, Ship's Council",
Citizens of Divinity's Reach,
"Citizens of Kaineng,

Due largely in part to increasing fears related to violence between the local Am Fah and Jade Brotherhood gangs, the Celestial Ministry is in debate over issuing a temporary nighttime curfew in the following city sectors: Vizunah Square, Wajjun Bazaar, and Bukdek Byway.

This is a direct reaction to the incident at Wajjun Bazaar last week, where eight individuals were killed near the marketplace. Of the dead, it was determined that six of the individuals were affiliated with the gangs, while two were unarmed civilians simply caught in the fray. Although the exact cause of this incident is still unknown, such violence will not be tolerated.

While investigations continue, please be mindful during daily activities and avoid unnecessary travel.

Flames, guide us.

Signed, Minister Zal",
Citizens of Rata Sum,
"Citizens of Tyria and Friends of Lion's Arch:
The karka remain a threat to our homes and our livelihoods. By order of Commodore Lawson Marriner, Captain Magnus Irondawn, and the entire Captain's Council, we hereby request any and all able-bodied adventurers to assist us in taking control of the island known as Southsun Cove and neutralizing the karka threat. If you wish to join us, please report to the Sanctum Harbor docks in Lion's Arch.
—Inspector Ellen Kiel",
"Citizens of Tyria:

The Lionguard has identified the person behind the recent animal attacks on Southsun Cove, but we need help bringing in the culprit. Our target is Canach, a secondborn sylvari with a history of stirring up trouble on Southsun Cove. Canach is already a wanted fugitive, but this latest round of mayhem has pushed him to the top of our most wanted list. Report to Southsun Cove if you're interested in helping me bring him to justice.

—Inspector Ellen Kiel",
