"Divo,  

You have my scripts, my final work before I take to the ramparts of our star. Were it so simple, I would go on living as a maestro of the page, but regrettably, sometimes one must trade the quill for the sword. All of my pent-up frustration towards the doyen and his diplomatic blunders over the years will have to live on in my words and your performance.  

I cannot show you greater adoration than your maker, Gardesano, who so loved you all, but in leaving you this play, know that it is an affirmation of all you've learned under my tutelage. Divo, my understudy, my primo uomo, let those who find this place know the fate that has befallen our world, and the hubris that lead us here.  

My blessings,  
Lodrizio
",
