More Stench Needed,
More Than She Bergen For—Snargle Goldclaw,
More Tracked Achievements,
More Trouble at Fort Salma,
More baubles for your troubles.,
"More detailed examinations made of the key structures today. The style shares similarities with the few other seer examples we have, but while those showed evidence of integration with other early Tyrian cultures, the designs here are truly unique. It'll take time to ascertain their precise age, but it looks like these really do predate everything else we've found before.  
 
And yet, they appear even more complex and detailed than the structures that came later. This suggests a decline in craftsmanship, but why? Possible theories: 
 
1. The mainland examples represent a divergent group of seers who broke off and lived separately and thus developed a different culture.  
  
2. The mainland examples we've found were from a remnant of the overall culture that survived for an undetermined period after the destruction of their civilization.  
  
3. The mainland examples are really just evidence of non-seers adapting the ruins for their own purposes.  
  
Further study will be needed to determine which of these hypotheses is most likely.",
More efficient at gathering resources and uncovering rare components.,
"More fleshstalkers breached the mountain pass—the stench reached our noses as the first scream sounded. Something about the breeze told me that the rest of the world was quaking, too. Surely we are not the only ones to endure these beasts...  
  
When wind carried the smell of blood back to the delta, my mind shot to the years prior. The frigid air that swept through the mountains. The lines of smoke, billowing from bonfires on the horizon. And then the disappearance of those lines as each outpost was demolished by the ice spawn... The bearkin bodies, stacked higher than the peat harvest.",
"More karka problems: the latest reports from Kessex Hills describe an all-out attack like the one we experienced in Lion's Arch. It's focused on Garenhoff, and we need to keep it contained there. If you can lend a hand, report to Garenhoff as soon as possible. And be careful: the local wizard's tower is involved in some strange occurrences of its own.
Good luck,
—Inspector Ellen Kiel",
More of Qadim's Top-Tier Supplies,
"More than ten years ago, the launch of Guild Wars 2 opened a new window into the world of Tyria. Five expansions, five seasons of Living World releases, and countless updates later, we're still inspired by the dedication of the game's fans.

To celebrate the occasion, please enjoy boosted rewards during this event! If you missed the tenth anniversary, it's also never too late to tackle the Decade of the Dragons achievements for a celebratory armor set and rewards. Your characters will also be receiving a small yearly gift as they reach their own birthday milestones.

It's an honor to share this world with you. Thanks for playing, and here's to many more years of adventuring in Tyria!

—ArenaNet",
