"Observe the Paper Lanterns  
  
Select the true statement from the choices below and follow its instructions:  
  
A red lantern is always next to a yellow lantern.  
  
The drop is inside the house that's located down the street on the right. Look behind the red armchair on the second floor.  

---
  
There are more than nineteen yellow lanterns but fewer than twenty-two.  
  
Continue down the street. Turn right and pass through the garden arch. Turn right again and continue straight down the street. Look behind the last crates.  

---
  
Blue lanterns are the rarest of them all. 

Backtrack toward the location of the first note. Go down the stairs on your right. Once down them, look to the right of the door.  
  
—CB",
