"The jaguar is a silent predator, capable of sneaking up on an unsuspecting foe and unleashing a deadly ambush. When not rending prey with their claws, jaguars also enjoy playing with colorful fabrics and shiny objects. —Acht",
"The jotun Korag is leading his people to ruin by following the ice dragon's dark path. Unless he is stopped, Korag's entire tribe will pay the price for his arrogance and be consumed by the dragon's corruption.",
"The journey continues, ten years after we embarked!",
"The journeykin eat much, and so they produce much scat. Picking it up and taking it to compost would be much appreciated.",
"The jungle is brimming with those...creatures. Demonic, smelly, and revolting. Just...gross. They're ruining this forest. I've made a habit of killing them on sight to help preserve the jungle, but they return every morning.   
  
I was complaining about my quandary over our nightly supper fire when a traveler said the beasts took on an entirely new form when he encountered them in the Shiverpeaks a week or so ago—he also called them ""titans,"" so at least I have a name to spit now. While these titans have taken on the jungle's mossy disguise, titans in the north are mimicking the icy mountain surroundings. Not only are they invasive, they are clearly very adaptive. I don't envy a lesser hunter trying to take one down, but I worry about what might happen if one crawled into a volcano...or a geyser.",
The karka have attacked Lion's Arch. Speak to Head Researcher Levvi or Inspector Ellen Kiel in Lion's Arch to respond to the karka threat.,
The karka have surfaced in Caledon Forest and Lion's Arch. Speak to Head Researcher Levvi or Inspector Ellen Kiel in Lion's Arch to learn more.,
