Those we love are never truly gone.,
"Those who retrace their steps may have audience with Turai Ossa, but he will soon leave.",
"Though Olaf Olafson was a popular figure amongst the norn community of  Drizzlewood, his success was at times a source of jealousy. One specific incident involves norn farmer and former Olafson friend Ike Ikeson. Ikeson frequented Olafson's gatherings, even attending several dinners hosted by the Olafson family. However, after hearing rumors of Olafson hiding his valuables in an undisclosed vault, Ikeson's greed overtook him. He strategically attended Olafson social events with the goal of siphoning clues about the treasure's whereabouts. After a neighbor informed Olafson that he caught Ikeson trying to break into the barn housing his sword, Olafson alleviated the problem by stabbing Ikeson through the abdomen with it, thereby damaging the friendship.",
"Though it may look bizarre, this tapir is a good-natured creature and an amiable companion. Its unassuming appearance hides a ferocious side, though, and siamoths are known for sending their opponents flying with a well-placed charge. —Acht",
"Though it may not seem like much, the trading we did with those jotun will make a lasting impact on their tribes. Hopefully they will learn from this experience and continue to trade peacefully with each other for years to come.

As an added bonus, the runic bloodstones that we received will go a long way toward our efforts in reading the ancient jotun languages. We just might decipher the ancient jotun texts yet!

—Albin Chronicler
Durmand Priory",
"Though its tenders are gone, the remains of a wondrous garden still shimmer with light in wild lands.",
"Though trouble may follow me, I overcome it with charm.",
"Though trouble may follow me, I overcome it with dignity.",
"Though trouble may follow me, I overcome it with ferocity.",
