"Well, I'll be darned—I actually finished everything on my to-do list. Unbelievable! The Tyrian Alliance gives you their deepest gratitude. Almost as deep as mine!",
"Well, looks like we've hit a dead end. The portal puzzle was a clever idea for an intelligence test—Blish really knows what he's doing with the portal tech. Unfortunately, it looks like the specimens aren't showing any special intellectual capacity. I wasn't the only one expecting positive results due to the Balthazar energy absorbed by Kralkatorrik.

A note: I'm starting to worry about housing the Branded specimens here. It's not just that they're extremely aggressive. I think there's strategy involved in their behavior. The other day, it really seemed like they were trying to trick me into leaving my notes in their lockup—notes that include the codes to the locks. Am I being paranoid?

A thought: maybe we should be testing their strategic/tactical capacities rather than their intellect?",
"Well, well. You've certainly earned my attention, %str1%.

What do they call you...the commander, was it? What a prestigious title. I've decided to make a special side project out of you, my dear. We're going to be seeing much more of each other, so you might as well cozy up and listen.

I warned you not to get in my way, but here we are. Next time I won't be quite so...gentle.

I simply can't wait to take you apart and see what makes you tick.

Tick-tock-tick.

—Scarlet (I don't need to hide behind silly codenames like ""B"" anymore, do I? This is quite exciting...)",
"Well, you've earned as much as I can pay you. Why don't you stop by to collect your reward? If you're looking for more work, I suspect you'll come in handy on the Diessa Plateau. We have real problems out on the range.

—Maxtar Rapidstep, Bovaris Estate",
